# Netlify proxy rewrites: keep the Supabase edge-function origin out of the
# customer-facing snippet. The widget.js runs from this same host, and without
# a data-api-url attribute it resolves its API base from the script's origin,
# so these routes must be proxied (status 200) to the edge functions.
#
# The widget only calls these three endpoints directly from the browser:
#   GET  /widget-config?chatbot=...
#   POST /chat
#   POST /feedback
# (products/orders/knowledge are invoked server-side by the chat agent.)
#
# Status 200 = surgical proxy rewrite: method, body and query string are
# forwarded; response headers (incl. Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *) pass
# through from the edge functions.
/widget-config  https://xsegdfcqqktxoqlbazpl.supabase.co/functions/v1/widget-config  200
/chat           https://xsegdfcqqktxoqlbazpl.supabase.co/functions/v1/chat           200
/feedback       https://xsegdfcqqktxoqlbazpl.supabase.co/functions/v1/feedback       200
/conversation-sync https://xsegdfcqqktxoqlbazpl.supabase.co/functions/v1/conversation-sync 200
